[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922002692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116438#issuecomment-3922002692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116438","id":3922002692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pxQME","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T17:02:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T17:02:18Z","body":"Hello! I feel like Godot is trying to interpret the value as a signed 64 bit integer, because that's the type that's used to store integers in Godot variables, and since it's not a valid *signed* 64 bit integer (but it's a valid *unsigned* 64 bit integer) Godot shows an error. See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/36387 .","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922002692/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922141731","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116438#issuecomment-3922141731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116438","id":3922141731,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pxyIj","user":{"login":"RevolNoom","id":52204256,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjA0MjU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52204256?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom","html_url":"https://github.com/RevolNoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RevolNoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T17:25:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T17:25:54Z","body":"I have just read the discussion, and I am a little confused. qarmin said that \"Hex can only be only represented as unsigned int\", but as per https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/language/integer_constant.html#The_type_of_the_integer_constant, hex can be represented as signed. \nAlso, I disagree that 0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF is not a valid signed 64 bit integer. Isn't that how -1 is represented always?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922141731/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922220306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116438#issuecomment-3922220306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116438","id":3922220306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pyFUS","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T17:38:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T17:38:32Z","body":"I agree that -1 is represented as 0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF in memory for a signed 64 bit integer, but that doesn't seem to be the case for integer literals (i.e. writing `0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF` in code):\nC++ in Visual Studio:\n<img width=\"602\" height=\"92\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a535a78-51c7-4e95-ab1b-eef44fe6ca8a\" />\nC# in Visual Studio:\n<img width=\"582\" height=\"138\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4be7b9fc-306c-45d5-8867-b7e02a97064d\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922220306/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,